Z||000000||80's BOY||06-16-2000||01:34 PM||||has anybody done this? i have in my possession<P>1) mustang 19# injectors<P>2) fuel rail adj. pressure regulator<P>3) 1988 iroc z fuel pump (new)<P>i'm hoping to gain SOME performance with all these changes. where is a good starting point for the pressures after installation? there isn't a dyno for 100 miles around here. also, what should i expect as far as driveability? curious to know everyone's opinion. should i get a chip too? ||||reg||5
Z||000001||olympic||06-16-2000||02:37 PM||||  Uuuummmm, installing bigger injectors and fuel pump won't do squat for HP on a stock engine.  You need to push more air AND fuel into an engine to make more power.  You should't need to upgrade the f/i's or pump unless you've done some serious head/cam mods or added forced induction or nitrous.||||reg||1
