Z||000005||ThatRickGuy||06-16-2000||04:13 PM||||Sounds like a nice set up, but like it was stated, the optimum fuel:air ratio is 1:16, that means if you're pushing more fuel, you have to push more air. And then, in order to get the fuel/air into the chamber, a longer duration or higher lift cam would really help, and then some of those sprint headers to help get the exess exhaust out. which would give you a very well rounded and powerful engine if you could get it tuned right. you already have most of that, the only thing I would suggest is a larger intake. there was a brutal one on ebay a while ago, a mod'd corvette intake... sweet.<P>oh, there may be one last hurdle... the computer, if the cam is just a little to wild, expecially in the overlap duration, the computer will fight the heck out of it and the car will run very poorly.||||reg||1
